 "evidence_tier": "3 (source review: every literal of PScore_test.cpp and AScore_test.cpp transcribed, including the six AScore::compute results over the four DTA inputs and the unambiguous case) plus 4 (native refusals and definition-derived invariants, marked 'native' in the test)",
 "openmp": "No #pragma omp in PScore.cpp or AScore.cpp; the port is serial, as the source.",
 "notes": [
  "PScore.cpp defines massCorrectionTerm, cleavageCorrectionTerm and modificationCorrectionTerm as free functions in namespace OpenMS, not as the PScore:: static members the header declares; the members have no definition and a call fails to link. The Rust associated functions carry the free functions' bodies.",
  "The vector overload of PScore::computePScore uses p = level / mz_window, the single-spectrum overload p = (level + 1) / mz_window; both are kept.",
  "AScore::computeCumulativeScore_ delegates to Math::binomial_cdf_complement (Boost incomplete beta upstream); the port uses concept::math_functions::binomial_cdf_complement, whose agreement with the source is recorded at that function."
